  "limitations": [
    "An alt-az antenna with no pointing offset has an exactly zenith boresight, where the parallactic angle is undefined; Section 4.2.1 refuses that case rather than approximating it, so the retained rotating-mount geometry row supplies a boresight altitude away from the pole and the degeneracy itself is retained only as a rejection.",
    "Backend parity covers the CPU-only JAX build and Dask over NumPy; no accelerator device was exercised, consistent with PERF-001.",
    "Config-case, rejection-probe, solver and backend-parity input digests are taken over the canonicalized document, with the volatile temporary workspace prefix replaced by the literal <workspace>, so each digest names the scientific input rather than the host path.",
    "The retained commands are the Stage-2 focused pytest module set, ruff lint, ruff format --check, and the docstring doctests; the remaining Section 9 gates (whole unit and integration suites, typecheck, the docs build, and the Tier-8 release acceptance module) are not retained here.",
    "This record was measured and generated on macOS x86_64 under Rosetta 2 using the locked osx-64 environment, because Section 8.1's extended-width predicate is unsatisfiable on the project's default osx-arm64 environment where NumPy longdouble aliases float64 and complex256 does not exist."
  ],
